-- §16  How much of each contract the difference guarding it is actually about.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ THE SAME READING AS §15, ONE LEVEL UP. There a zero column is a layer outside a
# relation's image; here it is a subject the population never reached, so the only thing putting
# it into the produced side is the roster the produced side is being compared against.
#
# ⛔⛔ AND IT IS WHY reports/coverage.sqlc AND THIS ONE MOVE IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS ON ONE EVENT.
# On the `rules` row the subjects short are the rules coverage calls ⛔ VACUOUS, by construction
# rather than by coincidence: both read `violates IS NOT NULL` over checks/all.sqlc. So a filing
# that gives one of them rows improves coverage and takes a subject away from here, in one event.
# Neither table says that alone, and the crossing is the whole reason to print the pair.
#
# ⚠️ `ok` IS NOT ONE FACT. A contract whose population the contract did not write earns it;
# so does one built exactly like `rules` whose population is merely complete today. The two are
# a template apart and a query cannot tell them apart at all, which is why examples/soundness.rs
# §5 exists beside this and not inside it.
#
# ⚠️ AND IT GRADES A DERIVED COLUMN RATHER THAN RESTRICTING ONE, which is a weaker thing than
# §15 is. `subjects - witnessed` is arithmetic over rank/guard_cover.sqlc's own counts and the
# verdict is a rendering, so nothing here is a second opinion about anything.
-- rank/guard_cover.sqlc, with the shortfall derived and named.
SELECT c.contract                                  AS "contract!",
       c.subjects                                  AS "subjects!",
       c.witnessed                                 AS "witnessed!",
       c.subjects - c.witnessed                    AS "roster_only!",
       CASE WHEN c.subjects = c.witnessed THEN 'ok'
            ELSE '⛔ the roster puts these on both sides of the difference'
       END                                         AS "verdict!"
FROM (
    :compose(rank/guard_cover.sqlc)
) c
ORDER BY c.subjects - c.witnessed DESC, c.contract
